Z||000000||MickeyAsh||03-07-2001||03:23 PM||||Hey guys, I'm looking at exhaust options and I was wondering if anyone had installed the fiero store's ocelot exhaust system, and if so, how they liked the sound and performance. Also if anyone knows any flowmaster fits, that'd be appreciated as well. Thanks in advance.<P>-Sheep||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||03-07-2001||04:47 PM||||I had the Oscelot system on my yellow GT before I installed the 3.8 and flowmaster. It sounded pretty much like stock, maybe a little louder. The major disadvantage is that it is not stainless like the OEM system and it will rust. Mine was all rusty after just a year or two. Performance isn't too much better than stock unless your stock system is plugged up.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||c m west||03-07-2001||06:16 PM||||We can supply you with a Modified Flowmaster that we design specifically for the Fiero, also we have many exhaust options that you may want to look into - check out our webpage....<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
